From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000006 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: solarizeddev <info@solarized.dev>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 1970 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] dashdec: drop xmlCleanupParser() after each manifest parse

parse_manifest() ended every DASH manifest parse with xmlCleanupParser(),
libxml2's process-exit teardown, which the library documents as unsafe
while any other thread is using it: in libxml2 2.13 it pthread_mutex_destroys
the static global xmlDictMutex (and the globals/memory mutexes). Firedown
runs ffmpeg on several threads of one process, so two overlapping DASH
manifest parses raced: one finished and destroyed the mutex, the other
locked it from xmlDictFree() while tearing down its parser context, and
bionic's FORTIFY aborted the app ("pthread_mutex_lock called on a destroyed
mutex", 1.1.91 tombstone under avformat_open_input <- jni_extract_metadata).

Drop the call. Nothing leaks: xmlFreeDoc() and xmlReadMemory() already free
every per-document allocation, and xmlInitParser() allocates nothing that the
next parse would not re-create. Marker: FIREDOWN-DASH-XMLCLEANUP.
---
 libavformat/dashdec.c | varies

--- a/libavformat/dashdec.c
+++ b/libavformat/dashdec.c
@@ -1431,7 +1431,18 @@
 cleanup:
         /*free the document */
         xmlFreeDoc(doc);
-        xmlCleanupParser();
+        /* FIREDOWN-DASH-XMLCLEANUP: vanilla calls xmlCleanupParser() here.
+         * That is libxml2's process-exit teardown, documented as unsafe
+         * while any other thread uses the library: it destroys the static
+         * global mutexes (xmlDictMutex among them), so a second DASH
+         * manifest being parsed concurrently on another thread of this
+         * process (the capture-probe pool, the downloader, a live
+         * refresh_manifest) locks a destroyed mutex in xmlDictFree() and
+         * bionic aborts the process ("pthread_mutex_lock called on a
+         * destroyed mutex"). Nothing leaks without it: xmlFreeDoc() above
+         * frees the document and xmlReadMemory() its parser context, and
+         * xmlInitParser() allocates nothing that the next parse would not
+         * simply re-create. */
         xmlFreeNode(mpd_baseurl_node);
     }
 
